  "faq_heading": "Coquitlam schools: your questions answered",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The BC Ministry of Education and Child Care school list shows 53 schools with a Coquitlam street address: 47 public schools and 6 independent schools. It also shows 1 college or university campus. In that list, 9 schools marked as offering French Immersion, 4 alternate programs and 2 online schools."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public schools here are run by School District 43 (Coquitlam) and School District 41 (Burnaby). Count by district: School District 43 (Coquitlam): 46, School District 41 (Burnaby): 1."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Alternate programs, continuing education centres and online schools that have a street address sit under \"other public schools and programs\"; the level of every school is read from its name."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public secondary schools with a Coquitlam address: Cabe Secondary, Centennial Secondary, Gleneagle Secondary, Maples School Program, Pinetree Secondary and École Dr. Charles Best Secondary."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Ministry file marks these Coquitlam schools as offering French Immersion: Our Lady of Fatima, École Banting Middle, École Dr. Charles Best Secondary, École Maillard Middle, École Montgomery Middle, École Nestor Elementary, École Panorama Heights Elementary, École Porter Street Elementary and École Rochester Elementary."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Independent schools listed for Coquitlam include Children of Integrity Montessori, Greater Heights Learning Academy, Our Lady of Fatima, Queen of All Saints Elementary, Royal Bridge High School and Traditional Learning Academy."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Before an offer, ask the district which school serves the exact street address."
    },
